      "id": "documentation",
      "disposition": "passed",
      "evidence": "integration:pose-mcp/go/calendar-date-skew-integration",
      "rationale": "The frontmatter reference now states that POSE stamps dates in UTC and what the gate tolerates, next to the rules it already listed. The helper comment gives the concrete 23:30 UTC-3 case, and the changelog fragment names the refusal readers met. The quickstart page needed no edit: its instruction to fill completed_at by hand is now correct in every zone."
    },
    {
      "id": "operability",
      "disposition": "passed",
      "evidence": "integration:pose-mcp/go/calendar-date-skew-integration",
      "rationale": "The failure an evaluator met on the documented first loop, and that made two CI gates depend on the hour and zone of the machine, is gone: quickstart and demo complete at 23:50 UTC-3 where they failed at 23:33. A genuine regression of two or more days is still an error with the same message."
    },
    {
      "id": "requirements",
      "disposition": "passed",
      "evidence": "integration:pose-mcp/go/calendar-date-skew-integration"
    },
    {
      "id": "scope",
      "disposition": "passed",
      "evidence": "structure:design-2a2867db4a111e3a",
      "rationale": "One comparison helper, its use in the spec gate and the knowledge check, one test, one doc paragraph and the registered producer. Stamping local dates was considered and rejected in D1; no stamp site was touched."
    },
    {
      "id": "security",
      "disposition": "passed",
      "evidence": "integration:pose-mcp/go/calendar-date-skew-integration",
      "rationale": "The change widens a date-order check by one day between two values parsed by the existing strict ISO parser. No input reaches a path, command or message it did not reach before, and no authorization or trust decision reads these dates."
